# Raw data: never versioned. It is downloaded from the source cited in the README
# and saved under the exact filename the scripts expect.
# Naming convention (phase 2):  origen_tema_periodo_version.csv
#
# This case: four SBA 7(a) FOIA extracts, ~860 MB in total. Downloaded from
#   https://data.sba.gov/dataset/7a-504-foia
# and saved as  sba_7a_<periodo>_2026-06-30.csv  under datos/crudos/.
datos/crudos/*.csv

# Keep small reference sources that DO belong in the repo by un-ignoring them
# explicitly, one line each.
#
# The SBA performance tables are transcribed from PDF, not redistributed: the source is
# a zip of eleven PDFs and only three numbers per year are used. Same treatment the
# football case gave FIFA's census — transcribe with citation, link the original.
!datos/crudos/sba_desempeno_2016-2025_2025-06-30.csv

# Derived datasets: regenerated by `python notebooks/procesar.py`.
#
# Note the trailing /* instead of /: git does not descend into an excluded directory,
# so `datos/limpios/` followed by `!datos/limpios/.gitkeep` would never re-admit the
# file and the folder would not reach a new repo at all. Ignoring the CONTENT keeps
# the exception reachable.
datos/limpios/*
!datos/limpios/.gitkeep
datos/intermedios/*
!datos/intermedios/.gitkeep

# OS / environment junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/

# graft's local graph cache — regenerable, not committed (run `graft build`).
graft/

# Video (video/README.md): the voice is personal and the music's licence forbids redistributing
# the file; renders are outputs. The published video is the public form of all of them.
# Any recording, whatever its name: takes were once saved as "Part 1.wav" … "Part 5.wav".
video/*.wav
video/musica*.mp3
video/composicion/voz_limpia.wav
video/composicion/mezcla.wav
video/composicion/transcript.json
video/composicion/renders/
# Generic agent instructions that `hyperframes init` writes into every project.
video/composicion/CLAUDE.md
video/composicion/AGENTS.md
